The change meets the task and the definition of done as far as the diff and a grep of the non-test code show. Only `listInvites` and `createInvite` return invite data to clients, and both use `inviteView`, which omits the token and hash. The plaintext token is set only on the copy `CreateInvite` returns, so it reaches the email and nothing else. Accept checks run in the right order: revoked gives 404, accepted gives 410 `invite_used`, and past `CreatedAt + 7d` gives 410 `invite_expired`. The 7-day boundary is inclusive, which matches "more than 7 days ago". Re-inviting revokes the older open invite case-insensitively, and the listing filters by `pending(now)`. Legacy snapshots are migrated in `FromState`.

Optional note, not a blocker: in `internal/store/types.go`, the `CreatedAt`, `AcceptedAt` and `RevokedAt` lines keep their old column alignment after the new `LegacyToken` field, so `gofmt` would realign that struct. Lint passed, so this is cosmetic.

